<gidredirect oldgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2013-01-15a.186.0" newgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2013-01-15b.186.0" matchtype="changes"/>
<speech id="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2013-01-15a.186.0" speakerid="uk.org.publicwhip/member/40573" speakername="Jeremy Lefroy" colnum="186"  time="009:30:00" url="http://www.publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm201213/cmhansrd/cm130115/halltext/130115h0001.htm#13011547000218">
	<p pid="a.186.0/1">I just want to point out the importance of the Government&#8217;s regional growth fund. In the case of Alston&#8212;I have already mentioned Alston, and I would be grateful if the Minister could visit it to see for himself the impact of the RGF&#8212;the fund has been used to invest in world-beating high-voltage direct current technology. For instance, last year Alston received an order worth 250 million euros from the Swedish grid, even in the face of stiff Swedish opposition.</p>
</speech>
